@scene chapter_6_riddle_weaver

background: night_valley.avif
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"West, as the Cataloguer said, the land turns strange and soft."
"Threads of light hang in the air like spider-silk, and every one is strung with tiny glowing runes."
"At the centre of the web sits a woman at an enormous loom, weaving the threads into sentences and unpicking them again."

background: riddle_weaver

npc Riddle Weaver:
"A traveller of letters, letter by letter, arrives —"
"— though not yet lettered enough to read the letters, I'd wager."

npc You:
"...I didn't understand a single word of that."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"No. Not yet. But you will — thread by thread."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE RIDDLE WEAVER"
"Weave a name from the ribbon of runes."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"Words are not LUMPS, child. They are RIBBONS."
"A ribbon of runes, each in its place — first rune, second, third — a line you can cut."

dialogue:
"She plucks a single thread from the loom. Runes run along its length, bright and small and ordered."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"Take only the runes you want. A SLICE, from here to there, and the rest falls away."
"The first few runes of a long word — cut them free, and you may hold a truer, shorter name hidden inside it."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"And when you have your name, you do not merely SHOW it, cold and bare."
"You WEAVE it — into a sentence, a greeting, a key. A thread of your own words wrapped snug around the name you found."

dialogue:
"Ahead, a final gate stands sealed. Across its face, a long ribbon of runes waits to be read."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"The gate hides a name inside a longer word — its first four runes, no more."
"Slice the name loose. Then weave it into the words that open the way:"
"'The gate opens for —' and then the name, and then a full stop, like a knot tied off."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Slice the first 4 runes as the name, then weave it into: The gate opens for {name}."

mission: riddle_strings

dialogue:
"You cut the first four runes loose. They hang shining in the air — a name, at last."
"Then you wrap your own words around them and speak the woven sentence aloud."
"The runes across the gate rearrange themselves to match — and the gate, at last, swings open."

background: night_forest.avif

dialogue:
"Beyond it, far up a leaning tower on the bare rock, a single window burns gold."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"There. Cut, and woven, and spoken true."
"The lazy one lives up there — the Enchanter. He'll not thank you for climbing all this way."
"But he holds one last art none of the rest of us could teach: how to never do a thing twice."

dialogue:
"You set your eyes on the golden window high above, and begin to climb."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Riddle Weaver"
"Applied: string slicing · f-strings"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 50
achievement: WEAVER OF NAMES

next:
chapter_6b_loom_of_words
